\b SMARTFLEET Project Summary & Updates\b0\par
\par
\b Project Capabilities (Current)\b0\par
1. Role-based login: Admin, Manager, Driver.\par
2. Admin: manage managers and drivers, block/unblock users, view all trips.\par
3. Manager: add/manage vehicles, assign/unassign drivers, create trips, view completed trips reports.\par
4. Driver: view assigned trips, accept/reject, complete trips with vehicle condition data.\par
5. Predictive Maintenance: on trip completion, model predicts maintenance requirement; vehicle status updates; manager alert created.\par
6. Notifications: driver gets trip assignment notifications; manager gets maintenance alerts.\par
7. Reports: completed trips with filters and CSV export.\par
\par
\b Teacher Requested Updates\b0\par
A. Add deliverable item details (not just load weight).\par
B. Add a payment system concept for driver support/settlement.\par
\par
\b Update A: Deliverable Item Details\b0\par
Purpose: record exact items being delivered for trip verification, auditing, and proof of delivery.\par
Proposed fields per trip: item name, item category, quantity, unit weight, total weight, handling notes, fragile flag.\par
Implementation options:\par
- Simple: add a text field "Items List" on trip creation and completion.\par
- Structured: create a TripItem table linked to Trip (1 trip -> many items).\par
Benefit: improves traceability and matches real logistics use cases.\par
\par
\b Update B: Payment System (Purpose & Suggested Design)\b0\par
Why it is useful:\par
- Drivers are often paid per trip, per km, or per delivery; system can compute and log it automatically.\par
- Allows reimbursement for tolls, fuel receipts, or extra handling.\par
- Enables payment transparency for management and drivers.\par
\par
Suggested approach (simple and explainable):\par
1. Trip completion captures delivery distance/time.\par
2. System computes driver payout using a fixed rate (e.g., per km or per trip).\par
3. Manager verifies and marks payment as approved/paid.\par
4. Driver can view payment status in dashboard.\par
\par
Optional fields:\par
- payment_amount, payment_status (pending/approved/paid), approved_by, approved_at.\par
- reimbursement_amount (if needed).\par
\par
\b Next Actions (If Implementing)\b0\par
1. Add TripItem model (or Items List field).\par
2. Add payment fields + simple payout calculation logic.\par
3. Add UI sections in Manager/Driver dashboards for items and payment status.\par
